  "appliesTo": "Governing bodies are responsible for setting the term and holiday dates for their schools. This calendar provides a framework to support governing bodies in determining those dates.",
  "academyNote": "Individual school dates may vary, so parents and carers should check the relevant school's website for confirmed dates.",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "In Newham, governing bodies set their own school's dates; the council calendar is a framework to support them.",
      "source": "https://www.newham.gov.uk/downloads/file/8985/school-term-and-holiday-dates-calendar-2026-2027"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The calendar provides 195 school days, and governing boards may add up to two more (a maximum of 197) for religious observance or to extend the Christmas or summer holiday.",
      "source": "https://www.newham.gov.uk/downloads/file/8985/school-term-and-holiday-dates-calendar-2026-2027"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Five INSET days should be identified by each school, either as full days or as an equivalent number of twilight sessions.",
      "source": "https://www.newham.gov.uk/downloads/file/8985/school-term-and-holiday-dates-calendar-2026-2027"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The calendar lists religious festivals, such as Diwali on Sunday 8 November 2026 and Eid ul-Fitr predicted to begin on the evening of Tuesday 9 March 2027.",
      "source": "https://www.newham.gov.uk/downloads/file/8985/school-term-and-holiday-dates-calendar-2026-2027"
    },
    {
      "fact": "For 2027-28 the council lists Eid ul-Adha on Friday 5 May 2028 and notes Islamic dates may vary by one day with moon sightings.",
      "source": "https://www.newham.gov.uk/downloads/file/11386/school-term-and-holiday-dates-calendar-2027-2028"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Both calendars describe themselves as a 'proposed calendar'.",
      "source": "https://www.newham.gov.uk/downloads/file/11386/school-term-and-holiday-dates-calendar-2027-2028"
    }
  ],
